<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
		The app half of the pair. It must match the extension's exactly:
		the shared keychain group is the only way the extension can read
		the payload key this app stores, because an extension runs in its
		own process with its own keychain partition.

		The group must be registered against the team in the Apple
		Developer account. Without that, everything compiles and the
		extension simply reads nothing — a failure that looks like a
		missing key rather than a missing entitlement.
	-->
	<!--
		APNs. Without this the app registers, Apple refuses, and the handset
		enrols poll-only - a failure that looks exactly like a missing
		Firebase project from the log.

		<b>"development" is right for every build this repo currently
		produces</b>, which are development-signed and sideloaded. A build
		signed with a distribution profile - TestFlight or the App Store -
		needs "production" here, and the value must match the profile: a
		mismatch is rejected at install rather than at build, and the message
		names neither side.

		Apple grants this to a paid Developer Program team only. A free
		personal team cannot sign an app that requests it at all, so a
		sideload on a free Apple ID fails outright rather than degrading -
		the same trap Link documents for Sign in with Apple.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)group.com.bleedingdeacons.hand</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>group.com.bleedingdeacons.hand</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
